         <name slugifiedName="name-accept">Accept</name>
         <t indent="0" pn="section-18.1-1">The Accept request-header field can be used to specify certain
 presentation description and parameter media types <xref target="RFC6838" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6838"/> that are
 acceptable for the response to the DESCRIBE request.</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-18.1-2">See Section 20.2.3 for the syntax.</t>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-18.1-2">See <xref target="section-20.2.3" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="Section 20.2.3"/> for the syntax.</t>
         <t indent="0" pn="section-18.1-3">The asterisk &quot;*&quot; character is used to group media types into ranges,
 with &quot;*/*&quot; indicating all media types and &quot;type/*&quot; indicating all
 subtypes of that type.  The range <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> include media type parameters
 that are generally applicable to that range.</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-18.1-4">Each media type or range <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> be followed by one or more accept-
-params, beginning with the &quot;q&quot; parameter to indicate a relative
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-18.1-4">Each media type or range <bcp14>MAY</bcp14> be followed by one or more accept-params,
+beginning with the &quot;q&quot; parameter to indicate a relative
 quality factor.  The first &quot;q&quot; parameter (if any) separates the media
 type or range's parameters from the accept-params.  Quality factors
 allow the user or user agent to indicate the relative degree of
 preference for that media type, using the qvalue scale from 0 to 1
 (<xref target="RFC7231" section="5.3.1" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7231#section-5.3.1" derivedContent="RFC7231"/>).  The default value is q=1.</t>
