         <name slugifiedName="name-detailed-list-of-changes">Detailed List of Changes</name>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-1">The below changes have been made to RTSP 1.0 (RFC 2326) when defining
-RTSP 2.0.  Note that this list does not reflect minor changes in
-wording or correction of typographical errors.</t>
-        <ul bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-i.2-2">
-          <li pn="section-i.2-2.1"> The section on minimal implementation was deleted.  Instead, the
-   main part of the specification defines the core of RTSP 2.0.</li>
-        </ul>
-        <ul bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-i.2-3">
-          <li pn="section-i.2-3.1"> The Transport header has been changed in the following ways:</li>
-        </ul>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-4"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  The ABNF has been changed to define that extensions are
-      possible and that unknown parameters result in servers ignoring
-      the transport specification.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-5"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  To prevent backwards compatibility issues, any extension or new
-      parameter requires the usage of a feature tag combined with the
-      Require header.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-6"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  Syntax ambiguities with the Mode parameter have been resolved.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-7"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  Syntax error with ";" for multicast and unicast has been
-      resolved.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-8"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  Two new addressing parameters have been defined: src_addr and
-      dest_addr.  These replace the parameters "port", "client_port",
-      "server_port", "destination", and "source".
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-9"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  Support for IPv6 explicit addresses in all address fields has
-      been included.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-10"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  To handle URI definitions that contain ";" or ",", a quoted-URI
-      format has been introduced and is required.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-11"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  IANA registries for the transport header parameters, transport-
-      protocol, profile, lower-transport, and mode have been defined.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-12"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  The Transport header's interleaved parameter's text was made
-      more strict and uses formal requirements levels.  It was also
-      clarified that the interleaved channels are symmetric and that
-      it is the server that sets the channel numbers.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-13"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  It has been clarified that the client can't request of the
-      server to use a certain RTP SSRC, using a request with the
-      transport parameter SSRC.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-14"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  Syntax definition for SSRC has been clarified to require 8HEX.
-      It has also been extended to allow multiple values for clients
-      supporting this version.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-15"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  Clarified the text on the Transport header's "dest_addr"
-      parameters regarding what security precautions the server is
-      required to perform.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <ul bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-i.2-16">
-          <li pn="section-i.2-16.1"> The Range formats have been changed in the following way:</li>
-        </ul>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-17"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  The NPT format has been given an initial NPT identifier that
-      must now be used.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-18"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  All formats now support initial open-ended formats of type
-      "npt=-10" and also format only "Range: smpte" ranges for usage
-      with GET_PARAMETER requests.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-19"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  The npt-hhmmss notation now follows ISO 8601 more strictly.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <ul bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-i.2-20">
-          <li pn="section-i.2-20.1"> RTSP message handling has been changed in the following ways:</li>
-        </ul>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-21"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  RTSP messages now use URIs rather than URLs.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-22"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  It has been clarified that a 4xx message due to a missing CSeq
-      header shall be returned without a CSeq header.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-23"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  The 300 (Multiple Choices) response code has been removed.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-24"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  Rules for how to handle the timing out RTSP messages have been
-      added.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-25"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  Extended Pipelining rules allowing for quick session startup.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-i.2-26"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-   *  Sequence numbering and proxy handling of sequence numbers have
-      been defined, including cases when responses arrive out of
-      order.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-        <ul bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-i.2-27">
-          <li pn="section-i.2-27.1"> The HTTP references have been updated to first RFCs 2616 and 2617
-   and then to RFC 7230-7235.  Most of the text has been copied and
-   then altered to fit RTSP into this specification.  The Public and
-   the Content-Base headers have also been imported from RFC 2068 so
